  "title": "Aspect pairs",
  "note": "Most verbs come in pairs. The imperfective is for processes, habits and repeated actions (Codziennie czytam gazetę). The perfective is for one completed action or result (Przeczytałem tę książkę). Perfective verbs have no present tense: their present-style forms mean the future (przeczytam = I'll read it through).",
